# The fixture corpus and the goldens are byte-exact artifacts. Git's
# end-of-line conversion would rewrite them on a Windows checkout, and the
# determinism check compares hashes across platforms -- a difference there has
# to mean the tool behaved differently, not that git edited its input.
testdata/fixtures/** -text
testdata/golden/** -text

# Shell scripts must keep LF wherever they are checked out; CRLF makes them
# unrunnable under bash.
*.sh text eol=lf

# The embedded SPDX templates are a gzip stream. Git detects that on its own,
# but end-of-line conversion on a Windows checkout would corrupt it silently
# and the failure would surface as licences that stopped matching.
*.gz binary
